  "interpretation": [
    "IT-MPPI, DIAL-MPC and CC-MPPI completed all 18 episodes in each protocol. These are small, paired scenario cohorts, not independent pooled trials or a general ranking.",
    "The selected Tsallis transform completed open/narrow/disturbance/mismatch but stalled in all two-route episodes and failed all S-turn episodes; one serial S-turn episode collided with the disk proxy. Finite support and higher ESS do not guarantee useful progress.",
    "Tube tracking corrections were active in S-turn under both protocols and in serial narrow passage. Robust sampled feedback was active only in S-turn. Earlier V03/V04 tracking inactivity is not generalized to all of V06.",
    "Robust planning includes candidate probes, paired rollouts and feedback design. Under the serial calibration it completed 12/18 episodes and missed 398/1726 command deadlines (23.06%). Its dynamics-work cohort completed 17/18, showing sensitivity to available samples without isolating a causal effect of feedback.",
    "All CC local terminal covariance bounds passed; empirical controlled-population terminal covariance violations were zero. Nonlinear prediction errors remain nonzero, and these sampling constraints are not guarantees for actual closed-loop state uncertainty.",
    "All dynamics-work commands respected the 7700-transition ceiling. Work-protocol timing includes concurrent load; use serial timing for hardware comparisons."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three evaluation seeds per scene/method/protocol, one tuning per method, and reused seeds across stages; no universal ranking.",
    "Finite-horizon local LQR replaces original iterative/contraction-guaranteed tracker designs. No tube, contraction or recursive feasibility theorem is reproduced.",
    "CC uses local linearization, zero initial auxiliary covariance, declared input noise, a finite terminal PSD tolerance and a 20% uncontrolled mixture outside the controlled bound.",
    "Wall-clock calibration is machine/load dependent and can select a minimum that already exceeds its target; it is not a hard deadline scheduler. Fixed simulated time does not model delayed actuation after misses.",
    "Existing simplified seven-state plant and centered disk collision proxy remain unchanged; full-body safety is not established.",
    "Success totals describe distinct executed conditions. External costs include failed/censored episodes and differ in duration; read completion and cost together."
  ]
